---
import Divider from './gb/Divider.astro';
---

<section class="section" id="model">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 class="headline">Two kinds of agent. One owner.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Give the agent that designs all the context it can hold. Give the agent that reviews none of
        it. The gap between the two is where design flaws surface, before they become code.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="pair">
      <article class="role">
        <div class="spot-badge">
          <img
            src="/images/spot-elephant.webp"
            alt="The Elephant agent holding blueprints and the Source of Truth scroll"
            class="spot-img"
            width="64"
            height="64"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </div>
        <h3 class="title">The Elephant</h3>
        <p class="role-sub">Remembers everything.</p>
        <p class="muted">
          Deep-context agents loaded with system history, architecture, component boundaries, and
          user journeys. The Elephant runs structured brainstorming, probes operational limits, and
          drafts the specification.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="role">
        <div class="spot-badge">
          <img
            src="/images/spot-goldfish.webp"
            alt="The Goldfish swarm reviewing technical plans and files"
            class="spot-img"
            width="64"
            height="64"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </div>
        <h3 class="title">The Goldfish</h3>
        <p class="role-sub">Remembers nothing.</p>
        <p class="muted">
          Stateless, isolated subagents that read only the draft spec and the live source, with none
          of the conversation&rsquo;s bias. A swarm of goldfish stress-tests the design from
          conflicting perspectives before any code exists.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <Divider />

    <div class="human">
      <div>
        <h3 class="title">The Human</h3>
        <p class="role-sub">Owns the outcome.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="muted">
        AI is an exploration partner and an automated auditor. Engineers own the architectural
        decisions, the trade-offs, and the result. Every design still goes to a person for review.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .pair,
  .human {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 32px clamp(32px, 6vw, 96px);
  }

  .pair {
    padding-block-end: clamp(40px, 6vw, 64px);
  }

  .human {
    padding-block-start: clamp(32px, 5vw, 48px);
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .pair,
    .human {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .role {
    max-inline-size: 48ch;
  }

  .spot-badge {
    inline-size: 64px;
    block-size: 64px;
    border-radius: var(--md-sys-shape-corner-md);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #fdfcf7;
    border: 1px solid var(--md-sys-color-outline-variant);
    margin-block-end: 24px;
    box-shadow: 0 1px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .spot-img {
    display: block;
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .role-sub {
    font: var(--md-sys-typescale-title-lg);
    letter-spacing: var(--md-sys-typescale-title-lg-tracking);
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant);
    margin-block: 2px 14px;
  }

  .human .muted {
    font: var(--md-sys-typescale-body-lg);
    max-inline-size: 56ch;
  }
</style>
